# Agent development standard

This repository adopts agent-standard without replacing its existing documentation.
The machine-readable contract is `.agent-standard/manifest.json`; repository-wide agent
instructions are in `AGENTS.md`.

Run the manifest `commands.verify` command before opening a pull request. Keep the
dependency lockfile and configured SBOM current together. Use an owned, reasoned,
expiring entry in `.agent-standard/waivers.json` only when the ordinary test policy
cannot apply.

The standard targets AS-3. Its manifest reports local and remote enforcement
separately; generated CI becomes a hard gate only after an administrator requires it
{% if repository_platform == 'github' %}in a GitHub ruleset{% else %}through an Azure Repos Build Validation policy{% endif %}.

{% if workflow_profile == 'spec-driven' -%}
Non-trivial changes use the OpenSpec workflow under `openspec/`.
{% else -%}
Record acceptance criteria in the pull request. For a non-trivial or high-risk change,
create a change plan from `docs/changes/0000-template.md`.
{% endif -%}
